# Reference: the five settings the requirements decide, then read back. A minute of acceptable loss is the log's job (everysec), the snapshot is
# for restarts and backups, noeviction makes a full box fail loudly instead of evicting a session, and the monitor is on before the incident.
# NOTE: the stack's own snapshot setting is "60 1000". The check reads "300 10", so it cannot be restored from this file: do
# CONFIG SET save "60 1000" after Verify (the grading harness does not reset save).
CONFIG GET save
CONFIG GET appendonly
CONFIG GET appendfsync
CONFIG GET maxmemory-policy
CONFIG GET latency-monitor-threshold
CONFIG SET save "300 10"
CONFIG SET appendonly yes
CONFIG SET appendfsync everysec
CONFIG SET maxmemory-policy noeviction
CONFIG SET latency-monitor-threshold 100
CONFIG GET save
CONFIG GET appendonly
CONFIG GET appendfsync
CONFIG GET maxmemory-policy
CONFIG GET latency-monitor-threshold
INFO persistence
